<p>President Trump said the United States would work with Iran to &quot;dig up and remove&quot; deeply buried nuclear material at sites struck by the US in June 2025, while also declaring that Iran would no longer enrich uranium. The new statements came as senior US officials sharpened demands for Iran to surrender its stockpile, with Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth saying Washington would &quot;get&quot; the material if Tehran did not hand it over voluntarily. Iran had not publicly confirmed Trump&#x27;s account of cooperation as of the reporting in the cited articles. At the same time, President Trump threatened 50% tariffs on countries that supply weapons to Iran, widening the pressure campaign beyond Tehran itself. The latest exchange shows the US combining diplomacy, military pressure and trade threats after last year&#x27;s strikes on Fordo, Natanz and Isfahan, with the immediate question now centered on whether Iran will accept outside removal of its enriched uranium stockpile and how other countries respond to the tariff threat.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Q6mCFCHH02sb-MzwvuT106eaVZa0Irqi5fmNvxVsXw6W1jb85g0Ks1b9jsUPVrLdswXtdPa9ASyWEclS8Ct4zhhiCjlyhjuZ14921T0rmdjZ' alt='US President Donald Trump speaks during the Future Investment Initiative summit in Miami Beach, Florida, on March 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Stockpile estimate: The New York Times reported US officials were focused on about 970 pounds of enriched uranium believed to be buried in Isfahan, a quantity central to the new demand for transfer or seizure.</li><li>Force option: The New York Times reported that Hegseth said Trump could still order a commando raid to seize the buried uranium if Iran refuses to transfer it, adding a specific military contingency to Washington&#x27;s demands.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump presented the situation as a new phase of engagement, saying the United States would work closely with Iran to remove buried nuclear material while insisting Iranian enrichment would end. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-says-u-s-will-work-with-iran-to-dig-up-enriched-uranium-iran-hasnt-confirmed-that'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth: Hegseth framed the issue as a compulsory transfer, saying the United States knows what Iran has and will obtain the uranium voluntarily or through force if necessary. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/08/world/middleeast/hegseth-caine-iran-uranium.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Iranian authorities: Iran had not publicly confirmed Trump&#x27;s claim that it would cooperate with the United States to excavate and remove enriched uranium, leaving a visible gap between Washington&#x27;s account and Tehran&#x27;s public position. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-says-u-s-will-work-with-iran-to-dig-up-enriched-uranium-iran-hasnt-confirmed-that'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Analysts cited by Al Jazeera: Analysts questioned the enforceability of the tariff warning, arguing that the legal basis for a 50% penalty on countries supplying Iran with weapons was not clear. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/8/trump-threatens-50-tariffs-on-countries-that-supply-iran-with-weapons'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-says-u-s-will-work-with-iran-to-dig-up-enriched-uranium-iran-hasnt-confirmed-that'>Trump says U.S. will work with Iran to &#x27;dig up&#x27; enriched uranium. Iran hasn&#x27;t confirmed that</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/8/trump-threatens-50-tariffs-on-countries-that-supply-iran-with-weapons'>Trump threatens 50% tariffs on countries that supply Iran with weapons</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/08/world/middleeast/hegseth-caine-iran-uranium.html'>Hegseth Demands Iran Turn Over Uranium Stockpiles</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990041/trump-declares-end-to-irans-uranium-enrichment'>Trump declares end to Iran’s uranium enrichment</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cnbc.com/amp/2026/04/08/trump-threatens-tariffs-countries-supplying-weapons-iran-ceasefire.html'>U.S. president Donald Trump threatens to impose 50% of tariffs on countries that supply military weapons to Iran.</a> - cnbc.com</li></ul>